														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1490547">
									

<p>I would think that being able to memorize and process at least 100 different equations on dozens of different objects, over and over again, without using paper or a calculator, would take a mathematical idiot-savant. If gaining that level of mathematical skill was part of the anomalous memetic effect, fine, but it should be noted. Also, a person who doesn't know what the various mathematical symbols mean shouldn't be affected, unless the anomalous memetic effect is granting knowledge of what they mean.</p>
<p>Finally, the use of the Σ notation in the equations is wrong. If you have something like &quot;Σ x&quot;, then under the Σ there should be &quot;x=[starting value]&quot;, and above it be &quot;[ending value]&quot;.</p>

							</div>

								
					
