														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1490699">
									

<p>The first problem I have with this is with the use of objective intelligence measurements. It's possible that the Foundation has some more advanced metrics to work with, but it seriously hurts my suspension of disbelief.<br />
Then there's the bit about people below the threshold having their intelligence boosted to the threshold in an objective, quantifiable way (as the result of a memetic attack, no less), that kicks my suspension of disbelief in the balls and runs away with its wallet.<br />
The bit at the end where O5 approves the use of an SCP object as a means to improve Class-D: no, bad author! No upvote! O5 wants to avoid cross contamination, not encourage it.</p>
<p>Beyond that, there are some tone issues. A significant portion of the article is devoted to describing the simulated universe, which feels a bit blunt and straightforward as far as SCPs go.<br />
In the end, it's a memetic DoS attack that kills you.</p>
<p>All that said, I would like to point out that it does show promise as a first article.<br />
-1</p>

